<!--
  The two entry shapes that break naive parsers, in one statement.

  Ntry 1 - INTERNAL batch booking (LSV+ collection).
     Ntry/Amt is the batch TOTAL of 1'500.00 and the three items appear as TxDtls
     (500.00 + 400.00 + 600.00). Summing entries and details together yields
     1'000.00 + 1'500.00 + 1'500.00 - 250.00 = 3'750.00 instead of 2'250.00, so the
     balance check below fails loudly the moment anyone double-counts.

  Ntry 2 - no NtryDtls at all (standing order).
     NtryDtls is 0..n; several Swiss banks deliver camt.053 with no transaction detail
     whatsoever. The entry is the whole truth and must still import.

  OPBD 1'000.00 + 1'500.00 - 250.00 = CLBD 2'250.00
-->
